  "name": "Schedule Instagram posts and Reels from a Google Sheets content calendar",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "dcc9e849-f78f-41a0-a4b2-f22c6bb3173b",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -700,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 960,
        "content": "## A content calendar in Google Sheets that schedules itself\nPlan Instagram posts and Reels in a sheet: date and time, caption, media link. Mark a row **ready** and it is scheduled in PostWire within 15 minutes. When the post goes live, the sheet gets the link; if Instagram refuses it, the row says why and you get an email. Instagram's API cannot publish later; PostWire keeps the queue.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Every 15 minutes** reads rows whose status is `ready`; **Valid rows only** skips rows without a media link, a time or a caption.\n2. **Schedule in PostWire** queues each row for its `publish_at` time (ISO 8601 with offset, e.g. `2026-10-10T18:00:00-05:00`).\n3. **Scheduled?** writes `scheduled` and the PostWire ID back to the row, or `error` with the fix and emails you.\n4. **When a post goes live or fails** (PostWire Trigger) fires when Instagram answers; **Went live?** writes `published` and the post link, or `failed` with the reason, to the same row.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the verified **PostWire** node (search \"PostWire\" in the nodes panel), create an account at postwire.io, connect your networks (one click each: no developer app, no Meta or TikTok review) and paste your API key into a **PostWire API** credential.\n2. Create a sheet with the columns `publish_at, caption, media_url, networks, status, schedule_id, post_url, note` and select it in all five Google Sheets nodes. `networks` is optional (default `instagram`; e.g. `instagram, facebook`).\n3. Media links must be public https links to the file, not a Drive share page. Add a Gmail credential, and your email in **Settings** and in **Email me what failed**.\n4. Activate the workflow: the trigger needs n8n at a public https address.\n\nFree PostWire plan: 20 posts a month and 2 networks per post, no card; 3 or more networks per post need a paid plan."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
